# Lua conventions

## Modules

- Dot paths from repo root: `require "word_game.ui.cards.letter_faces"`
- Package folders use `init.lua`
- Most modules: `local M = {}` … `return M`
- Pure data configs may `return { ... }` directly (`deck_face_colors.lua`)

## Naming

- Files/dirs: `snake_case`
- Locals: `snake_case`
- Classes/globals: `PascalCase` (`LetterTile`, `Game`, `Panel`)
- Package globals: `UPPER_SNAKE` (`WORD_GAME`, `WORD_GAME_UI`)
- Feature flags: `F_*` from `runtime_options.flags`

## Classes (`jumbalaya-engine/scene`)

```lua
LetterTile = AnimNode:derive("LetterTile")

function LetterTile:construct(X, Y, W, H, ...)
    EaseNode.construct(self, X, Y, W, H)
end
```

Chain: `Kind → SceneNode (Node) → Spatial (AnimNode / EaseNode) → Sprite, Panel, LetterTile, CardPile`

Spatial motion: `set_rect`, `follow(parent, offset)`, `bind_to(host)`. See `docs/engine.md` and remaining work in `docs/engine-lineage.md`.

`letter_tile.lua` mixes in presentation via `word_game/ui/cards/bind.lua`.

## Callbacks & layout

- Remaining string callbacks go through `Funcs.register` — move implementations, not registration names. New UI uses function `on_press`.
- Model requests layout via `WORD_GAME.Layout.request_refresh()` / deferred `G.ARGS.pending_layout` — not direct geometry from model code

## Annotations

Add `---@class` / `---@field` on new public APIs. Analyzer stubs live in `types/`; `.emmyrc.json` ignores `_tools/`.

## Do not hand-edit

`dictionary/words_set.lua`, regenerated `deck_face_colors.lua`, binary assets — use `_tools/` scripts.
